# Adding a Protocol to Deploy the Site

[`site:deploy`](../deploy-mojo.html) and [`site:stage-deploy`](../stage-deploy-mojo.html) copy the site with a [Wagon](/wagon/) provider chosen by the protocol of the site URL in `<distributionManagement>`. Out of the box, only `file:` URLs work: the plugin brings the file provider, and the HTTP provider that ships with Maven cannot copy a directory.

A URL with any other protocol fails. For example, with an `scp:` URL:

```
[ERROR] Failed to execute goal org.apache.maven.plugins:maven-site-plugin:${project.version}:deploy (default-cli) on project scratch-parent: Cannot find wagon which supports the requested protocol: scp -> [Help 1]
```

and with an `http:` URL:

```
[ERROR] Failed to execute goal org.apache.maven.plugins:maven-site-plugin:${project.version}:deploy (default-cli) on project scratch-parent: Wagon protocol 'http' doesn't support directory copying -> [Help 1]
```

To deploy with another protocol, add the [Wagon provider](/wagon/) for it:

| Site URL | Wagon provider |
|----------|----------------|
| `scp://`, `sftp://` | [`org.apache.maven.wagon:wagon-ssh`](/wagon/wagon-providers/wagon-ssh/) |
| `dav:http://`, `dav:https://` (WebDAV) | [`org.apache.maven.wagon:wagon-webdav-jackrabbit`](/wagon/wagon-providers/wagon-webdav-jackrabbit/) |

You can add it either as a [build extension](/guides/mini/guide-using-extensions.html), or declare it as a dependency of the Site Plugin:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <pluginManagement>
      <plugins>
        <plugin>
          <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
          <artifactId>maven-site-plugin</artifactId>
          <version>${project.version}</version>
          <dependencies>
            <dependency><!-- add support for scp and sftp -->
              <groupId>org.apache.maven.wagon</groupId>
              <artifactId>wagon-ssh</artifactId>
              <version>${wagonVersion}</version>
            </dependency>
          </dependencies>
        </plugin>
      </plugins>
    </pluginManagement>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

Credentials for the server go into a `<server>` element of your `settings.xml` whose `<id>` matches the `<id>` of the site in `<distributionManagement>`; see the [Guide to Deployment and Security Settings](/guides/mini/guide-deployment-security-settings.html).

To publish the site to a source control system, such as GitHub Pages or the Apache svnpubsub/gitpubsub service, use the [Maven SCM Publish Plugin](/plugins/maven-scm-publish-plugin/) instead of a Wagon provider: it commits all files in one commit, where the [Wagon SCM provider](/wagon/wagon-providers/wagon-scm/) commits each file separately. See [Deploying the Site](https://maven.apache.org/guides/mini/guide-site.html${esc.hash}GitHub_Pages.2C_Apache_svnpubsub.2Fgitpubsub_Deployment) in the site guide.
